1
00:00:00,298 --> 00:00:03,449
What if the world you know had never existed?

2
00:00:03,567 --> 00:00:06,307
What if Nazi Germany and Imperial Japan

3
00:00:06,347 --> 00:00:08,868
had won the Second World War?

4
00:00:08,908 --> 00:00:12,079
This is one possible alternate history.

5
00:00:14,384 --> 00:00:17,522
In our history, the Axis powers were defeated.

6
00:00:17,562 --> 00:00:22,767
Germany surrendered in May 1945; Japan, that August.

7
00:00:22,885 --> 00:00:25,205
Victory would have needed many changes,

8
00:00:25,245 --> 00:00:27,212
not one single battle.

9
00:00:27,287 --> 00:00:31,389
So imagine the war ending in an uneasy settlement.

10
00:00:32,064 --> 00:00:34,104
In this imagined world, Germany

11
00:00:34,144 --> 00:00:36,915
dominates much of continental Europe.

12
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:38,740
Japan holds vast territories

13
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:41,795
across East and Southeast Asia.

14
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:45,408
The United States remains a powerful rival.

15
00:00:46,383 --> 00:00:49,930
For millions in Europe, the nightmare would not end.

16
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:52,070
In real history, the Nazi regime

17
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:55,910
murdered six million Jews, and millions of others.

18
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,320
In a victorious Reich, persecution

19
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,042
and mass murder could have continued.

20
00:01:01,202 --> 00:01:03,842
Families displaced. Papers checked.

21
00:01:03,882 --> 00:01:05,749
Freedom of speech, gone.

22
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:09,984
Japanese rule in occupied Asia was also harsh,

23
00:01:10,024 --> 00:01:12,260
though it varied by place.

24
00:01:12,335 --> 00:01:15,595
Rice, rubber, oil and tin were taken.

25
00:01:15,635 --> 00:01:18,138
Hundreds of thousands were forced into labour.

26
00:01:18,298 --> 00:01:20,498
If that rule had lasted, exploitation

27
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:22,936
might have shaped generations.

28
00:01:23,011 --> 00:01:24,411
Yet people would still hold on

29
00:01:24,451 --> 00:01:27,295
to family, faith, and language.

30
00:01:27,970 --> 00:01:30,322
But would the victors stay friends?

31
00:01:30,362 --> 00:01:32,582
Germany and Japan were distant allies

32
00:01:32,622 --> 00:01:34,688
with different ambitions.

33
00:01:34,728 --> 00:01:36,588
Facing the United States, they might

34
00:01:36,628 --> 00:01:40,456
become three rivals: watching, arming, waiting.

35
00:01:40,496 --> 00:01:43,266
A different Cold War might have begun.

36
00:01:44,026 --> 00:01:47,577
Now, closer to home: Sarawak, on Borneo.

37
00:01:47,652 --> 00:01:50,732
This part is real: Japan occupied Sarawak

38
00:01:50,772 --> 00:01:54,231
from 1941 to 1945.

39
00:01:54,271 --> 00:01:58,149
People lived with shortages, strict control, and fear.

40
00:01:58,479 --> 00:02:02,128
Now imagine that occupation had never ended.

41
00:02:02,203 --> 00:02:05,773
Would Sarawak have remained under Japanese rule?

42
00:02:05,813 --> 00:02:09,953
In our history, it helped form Malaysia in 1963.

43
00:02:09,993 --> 00:02:11,614
Would that still happen?

44
00:02:11,689 --> 00:02:15,125
And what about our languages, families, and future?

45
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:18,140
History was never inevitable.

46
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:22,190
It was shaped by choices, sacrifice, and resistance.

47
00:02:22,265 --> 00:02:25,954
A different ending could have changed millions of lives.

48
00:02:26,199 --> 00:02:28,427
So, what would your world look like?

49
00:02:28,757 --> 00:02:31,692
What if history had turned the other way?

50
00:02:32,532 --> 00:02:36,283
And what if Sarawak had never left Japanese rule?

